{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.finiteKWitness_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.finiteKWitness_refl","kind":"instance","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L379-L385","doc":"**Self-agreement (reflexivity)**: when `f_k = f_k'`, the\nagreement bound holds with LHS = 0 ≤ tol (using `htol`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness.agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness.agreement","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L377-L377","doc":"Numerical agreement at `(k, k')`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L373-L373","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.FiniteKWitness","kind":"class","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L366-L377","doc":"**Finite-k witness — numerical agreement class.**\nPer-`(k, k', tol)` witness that the level-`k` and level-`k'`\nbranching fractions agree within tolerance `tol`. The `mpmath`\nwitness in `jet-knot-invariants.witness.json` records\n`|f_μ^{(k)} − f_μ^{(4)}| < 0.01` for k = 4, …, 9 across all\natoms tested; instances of this class are the formal record of\nthat numerical agreement at specific `(k, k', tol)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.finite_k_convergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.finite_k_convergence","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L350-L364","doc":"**Convergence at finite k** (the practically useful version).\n\nFor k = 4, ..., 12 (the BW formula range), the branching\nfractions are bounded by explicit constants computable from\nthe H_3(q) characters and the partition structure at each k.\n\nThis does NOT require k → ∞ asymptotics — it's a finite\nverification at each level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.branchingConverges_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.branchingConverges_refl","kind":"instance","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L341-L348","doc":"**Self-convergence (reflexivity)**: when `f_k = f_inf`, the\nbound holds trivially with LHS = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.branchingConverges_of_fact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.branchingConverges_of_fact","kind":"instance","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L331-L339","doc":"**Default instance from a `Fact` witness on the bound**.\nWhen `Fact (|f_k - f_inf| ≤ C_q / √(k-3))` is in scope (e.g.\nfrom a numerical witness at the specific `(k, f_k, f_inf)`),\nthe typeclass instance follows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges.bound","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L329-L329","doc":"The Féray–Méliot O(1/√k) bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges.mk","kind":"ctor","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L326-L326","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.BranchingConverges","kind":"class","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L319-L329","doc":"**Branching convergence — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nThe free-real statement `|f_k - f_inf| ≤ C_q / √(k-3)`\nhas no a-priori semantic link between `f_k`, `f_inf`, `C_q`,\nand the actual q-Plancherel branching fractions. Until the\nMathlib q-Plancherel CLT lands, callers must witness the\nbound for the specific `(k, f_k, f_inf, C_q)` they use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.hookWalkTransition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.hookWalkTransition","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L288-L302","doc":"**Kerov q-hook walk transition**.\n\nThe q-hook walk removes a corner cell c from λ with probability\nproportional to d_q(λ\\c)² × [hook(c)]_q / d_q(λ)².\n\nAfter k-3 steps of the reverse walk (adding cells from μ ⊢ 3\nup to λ ⊢ k), the accumulated weight gives the q-Plancherel\nbranching fraction.\n\nThe stationary distribution of the walk restricted to\npartitions of 3 IS d_q(μ)/Σd_q(ν) — this is the q-deformed\nlimit, confirmed by Kerov's analysis of the q-hook walk. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_alt","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L174-L178","doc":"Concrete verification at k = 4 for alternating rep:\nm_{(1,1,1)}: 0, 0, 0, 1, 1.\nΣ dim·m = 0 + 0 + 0 + 3 + 1 = 4.\nk!/6 · 1 = 4. ✓ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_sym","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L168-L172","doc":"Concrete verification at k = 4 for symmetric rep:\nm_{(3)}: 1, 1, 0, 0, 0.\nΣ dim·m = 1 + 3 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 4.\nk!/6 · 1 = 4. ✓ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_k4_std","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L158-L166","doc":"Concrete verification at k = 4:\nΣ dim(λ)·m_{(2,1)}^λ over λ ⊢ 4 = 4!/6 · 2 = 4·2 = 8.\n\nPartitions of 4: (4)→dim=1, (3,1)→dim=3, (2,2)→dim=2,\n(2,1,1)→dim=3, (1,1,1,1)→dim=1.\nm_{(2,1)}: 0, 1, 1, 1, 0.\nΣ dim·m = 0 + 3 + 2 + 3 + 0 = 8.\nk!/6 · dim(μ) = 24/6 · 2 = 8. ✓ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_identity_n3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_identity_n3","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L151-L156","doc":"The Fomin identity specialized to `n = 3`, as a predicate:\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ k} dim(λ)·m_μ^λ = (k!/6)·dim(μ)` (see `fomin_identity`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.fomin_identity","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L134-L149","doc":"Fomin identity (Fomin 1994), as a **predicate** on branching data:\nthe first-moment branching sum `Σ_{λ ⊢ k} dim(λ)·m_μ^λ` equals\n`(k!/n!)·dim(μ)`.\n\nNamed, not asserted (§3b): `dim_fn` / `mult_fn` here are arbitrary\nfunctions, so the equation is provable only once they are the genuine\nSYT counts `dim(λ) = #SYT(λ)`, `m_μ^λ = #SYT(λ/μ)` — the upstream\ncombinatorial input, not yet formalized here. The concrete instance\n`fomin_k4_std` below (`by decide`) verifies it at `k = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.ratio_perturbation_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.ratio_perturbation_bound","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L65-L77","doc":"Corollary: if the cross-term |B·C − A·D| is bounded by ε·C²,\nthen |f − A/C| ≤ ε · C/(C+D) ≤ ε. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.ratio_perturbation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchingConvergence.ratio_perturbation","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchingConvergence.lean#L49-L63","doc":"**Ratio perturbation lemma**: if f = (A + B)/(C + D) and\nthe \"unperturbed\" ratio is A/C, then:\n\n|f − A/C| ≤ |B·C − A·D| / (C·(C + D))\n\nprovided C > 0 and C + D > 0. ","signatureChunk":0}]}